  "question": {
    "text": "For the real parameter \\(t\\), the locus of the complex number \\(\\mathrm{z}=\\left(1-\\mathrm{t}^2\\right)+i \\sqrt{1+\\mathrm{t}^2}\\) in the complex plane is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "PoZY0",
      "text": "an ellipse",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "rME45",
      "text": "a parabola",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "6FKBG",
      "text": "a circle",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9rwK8",
      "text": "a hyperbola",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: Given \\(\\mathrm{z}=\\left(1-\\mathrm{t}^2\\right)+\\mathrm{i} \\sqrt{1+\\mathrm{t}^2}\\)\nLet \\(z=x+i y\\)\n\\(\\begin{gathered}\nx=1-t^2 \\\\\ny^2=1+t^2\n\\end{gathered}\\)\nThus, \\(x+y^2=2\\)\n\\(\\begin{aligned}\n& y^2=2-x \\\\\n& y^2=-(x-2)\n\\end{aligned}\\)\nThus parabola",
    "image": null
  },
